- [P2] Configure sticky phase before enabling post-sticky target — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/base/abci/abcStmap_94.c:131-131
  When `stmap94` is invoked normally, this only enables the emitted-drive target and moves it after `Map_Stmap82MaybeBlockStickyReplacement`; however that sticky blocker is a no-op unless `Map_Stmap82SetStickyParentPhase` has been configured. Since this command never enables/clears the sticky parent phase for `ParentAigId`/`ChildAigId`, the advertised post-sticky interaction is not exercised and `stmap94` effectively behaves like the prior emitted-drive target path for fresh runs.
